hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17610","Abu al-'Ala' al-Hasan ibn Sawwar narrated to us: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Mu'awiyah ibn Salih, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from his father, from Ka'b ibn 'Iyad, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Indeed for every nation there is a trial, and indeed the trial of my nation is wealth."
"17611","Ziyad ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us: 'Abbad ibn Kathir al-Shami, from the people of Palestine, narrated to us, from a woman among them called Fusaylah, who said: I heard my father say: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, is it part of tribal partisanship for a man to love his people? He said: No, but part of tribal partisanship is for a man to aid his people in wrongdoing."
